-- title:
--   Zariski-local freeness and two invariant generators of a subgroup ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B$ a commutative Noetherian ring in which $p$ is nilpotent, $X$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$ — that is, a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $B$ together with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2} = W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ by law endomorphisms and a law endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ a = \sigma(a)\circ\varpi$ — let $I$ be an ideal of $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ and $h$ a natural number. Assume: $B[\![x]\!]/I$ is finite and projective over $B$; for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f : B \to \kappa$ the quotient $\kappa[\![x]\!]/I\kappa[\![x]\!]$ has $\kappa$-dimension $p^h$; some power $q$ satisfies $x_i^q \in I$ for both variables; every element of $I$ has zero constant coefficient; for $f \in I$ the series $f(F(x,y))$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by $I(x) \cup I(y)$; and $I$ is stable under substitution by $a\cdot$ for each $a \in \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ and by $\varpi$. Then there are finitely many $g_1,\dots,g_n \in B$ generating the unit ideal such that, writing $B_i = B[1/g_i]$ and $I_i$ for the image of $I$ in $B_i[\![x]\!]$: $B_i[\![x]\!]/I_i$ is finite and free over $B_i$; some power $q$ satisfies $x_{i'}^q \in I_i$ for both variables; and there is a pair $u_1,u_2 \in B_i[\![x]\!]$ with zero constant coefficients, each satisfying $u_j(F(x,y)) - u_j(x) \in (I_i(y))$ over the base-changed law, and with $(u_1,u_2) = I_i$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the construction of the quotient of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module by a finite locally free infinitesimal $\mathcal{O}_D$-stable subgroup of order $p^h$: Zariski-locally on the base the subgroup algebra is free and the subgroup ideal is generated by two invariant series without constant term. It feeds [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_invariant_coordinates_of_subgroup_ideal`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_invariant_coordinates_of_subgroup_ideal) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.act_pow_mem_span_of_isODHom_of_hasKernelOfDegree`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.act_pow_mem_span_of_isODHom_of_hasKernelOfDegree).
